          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A 2023 materialized-view troubleshooting discussion clarifies that linking a Trigger data source links a cluster, whereas a Charts data source names a collection. Linking the cluster does not itself schedule a saved Charts aggregation. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/create-scheduled-trigger-using-atlas-charts-data-source/220164",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a64c17ac4185a0fa3ce1c566297abf88b421485d92571c8933ee5f5dc3b2d4db",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:10c3d5a291af9f32d91b851fc72af9cf1f2d718969e7b613022911ea894ddbda"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MongoDB recommends a $match filter to reduce the documents examined by a Scheduled Trigger Function and help avoid Function memory limits. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-ui/triggers/scheduled-triggers.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0810e20afe46dc3babb7e65cb87822dc8068f331be4699e01de30be87cc768a9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:917e7fe6e50bf1a13ad30565832a5a7a827635517dd6d6fb8196aa4874775f17"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A Scheduled Trigger can invoke a Function that aggregates orders and persists a daily report in another collection. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-ui/triggers/scheduled-triggers.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8faebb85ea5a8cb8e4109481f65483d7160cb8e4f9e8fdedd9477a2b35971c22",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
