    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "MongoDB's cross-collection tutorial recommends an Atlas Scheduled Trigger to rerun a materialized-view aggregation monthly in production; the schedule invokes refresh work rather than making stored results continuously current. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/search/tutorial/cross-collection-tutorials.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d18b6b4290a62b9600504cefcf66c8e24469ca566b286a28e3fb97edf61891da",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e4a3a82b4d313be9e5c690e3125a04b3a99b79e1b12f79a18c476eb684c827ec"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A Scheduled Trigger supplies no arguments to its linked Function. Refresh parameters therefore need to come from the Function's code or data it reads, rather than an assumed event argument. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-ui/triggers/scheduled-triggers.md",
          "note": null,
